      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="portfolio-grid case-study-layout">
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Project Overview</span>
              <h2>What the system does and why teams depended on it</h2>
              <p>Udigify is a digital product tool built for design teams and creative businesses managing repeat content production. The product was designed to replace scattered files and inconsistent review handoffs with a structured creative operations workflow.</p>
              <p>From an engineering perspective, the system had to organize large creative libraries, approval cycles, and workspace context while keeping retrieval and review fast. That made it a production platform with real operational demands rather than a portfolio demo.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Business Challenge</span>
              <h2>What had to improve for the product to scale cleanly</h2>
              <p>The core business challenge was delivering a product that could serve creative operations and digital asset management use cases while still remaining easy for operators to trust and use every day.</p>
              <p>The client needed a system that improved creative efficiency and reduced the wasted time caused by missing files, unclear versions, and fragmented review flows.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
